erge-review-5308c84e/security-review.events.jsonl\n/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/lies-users-julian-documents-codex-2026/work/local-merge-review-5308c84e/code-review.events.jsonl\n{\n  \"role\": \"code-review\",\n  \"head\": \"5308c84ee3fab34754ea71a2917be9ae19b19923\",\n  \"base\": \"ad92a0864ac56987a4896fd5770abab0c0c9b271\",\n  \"verdict\": \"request_changes\",\n  \"signal\": \"fail\",\n  \"summary\": \"The native monitor has unresolved finish-all recovery and authentication lifecycle defects. The supplied validation receipts do not establish CI success for this commit.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"path\": \"rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/native-monitor/group-monitor/test-session-manager/test-session-manager.service.ts\",\n      \"line\": 367,\n      \"title\": \"Retrying finish-all can leave connected tests unterminated\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Finish-all first locks the captured tests, then sends terminate after a delay. If the terminate request fails, the UI reports failure, but the locks have already committed. On retry, the fresh snapshot excludes every locked test from both lockIds and terminateIds, so the retry can succeed and navigate away without terminating those still-connected tests. The same gap occurs if the operation is interrupted after locking.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Make the operation recoverable across partial completion: retain or reconstruct the exact authorized termination targets after locking, and do not report completion until their termination requests succeed. Add coverage for a failed or interrupted terminate followed by retry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"path\": \"rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/native-monitor/native-monitor-entry.component.ts\",\n      \"line\": 54,\n      \"title\": \"Bind logout confirmation to the session that opened it\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The dialog subscription survives component destruction and calls session.logout() on whichever access is current when it closes. If the original access is cleared or the user navigates away and signs in again while the confirmation remains open, confirming the old dialog logs out the new session and navigates back to the monitor.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Capture the access identity when opening the dialog, cancel and close it when that access or component is retired, and verify the identity before logging out or navigating.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"path\": \"rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/native-monitor/native-monitor-entry.component.ts\",\n      \"line\": 48,\n      \"title\": \"Cancel pending login navigation when the entry view is retired\",\n      \"evidence\": \"submit awaits an unscoped login and then opens the sole claim. ngOnDestroy only unsubscribes from backend problems, so a delayed login or proof-of-work result can establish access and navigate back to the monitor after the user has left the entry view.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Tie login and its continuation to the entry view's lifetime; cancel or invalidate pending authentication on destruction and avoid applying or navigating from a retired attempt.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"verified\": [\n    \"Checked the actual base-to-head diff, current HEAD and tree, native monitor routes, session and request scopes, profile selection, signed-int64 serialization, polling, Booklet caching, controls, and relevant lifecycle tests against current source.\",\n    \"Compared the finish-all and login behavior with the named read-only Original checkout and inspected the checked-in monitor scope and qualification limits.\",\n    \"The supplied receipt reports completed base CI at ad92a086, historical published CI failures at 13b553, and later local evidence at fe4e882; none is a complete CI result for 5308c84. The cache-environment proof names 5d9ba6c as its pre-fix head.\",\n    \"Earlier reported Goto context capture, slow Booklet enrichment, profile cancellation and timer input issues have corresponding changes in current source; their historical failures alone are not treated as current findings.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"No current commit-matched CI or complete browser qualification was supplied, and broad suites were not rerun. Whole-project, visual and native participant transport parity remain unproven.\",\n    \"Findings are based on source and control-flow inspection; the partial finish and stale authentication scenarios were not reproduced in a browser during this review.\",\n    \"The repository Brain brief could not run because its lock directory could not be created in the read-only environment; direct source and documentation inspection was used instead.\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7875}},"started_at_ms":1793258604690,"completed_at_ms":1793258604690}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T07:23:24.693Z","ordinal":12678,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1868a-c895-7f83-8080-b6a1953196a9","call_id":"call_c607936b984e45348f3baeb7028c36f5","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"796eea\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1301,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/lies-users-julian-documents-codex-2026/work/local-merge-review-5308c84e/run.json\\n/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/lies-users-julian-documents-codex-2026/work/local-merge-review-5308c84e/security-review.schema.json\\n/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/lies-users-julian-documents-codex-2026/work/local-merge-review-5308c84e/code-review.schema.json\\n/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/lies-users-julian-documents-codex-2026/work/local-merge-review-5308c84e/code-review.json\\n/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/lies-users-julian-documents-codex-2026/work/local-merge-review-5308c84e/security-review.events.jsonl\\n/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-10-28/lies-users-julian-documents-codex-2026/work/local-merge-review-5308c84e/code-review.events.jsonl\\n{\\n  \\\"role\\\": \\\"code-review\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"5308c84ee3fab34754ea71a2917be9ae19b19923\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"ad92a0864ac56987a4896fd5770abab0c0c9b271\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"request_changes\\\",\\n  \\\"signal\\\": \\\"fail\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The native monitor has unresolved finish-all recovery and authentication lifecycle defects. The supplied validation receipts do not establish CI success for this commit.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/native-monitor/group-monitor/test-session-manager/test-session-manager.service.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 367,\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Retrying finish-all can leave connected tests unterminated\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Finish-all first locks the captured tests, then sends terminate after a delay. If the terminate request fails, the UI reports failure, but the locks have already committed. On retry, the fresh snapshot excludes every locked test from both lockIds and terminateIds, so the retry can succeed and navigate away without terminating those still-connected tests. The same gap occurs if the operation is interrupted after locking.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Make the operation recoverable across partial completion: retain or reconstruct the exact authorized termination targets after locking, and do not report completion until their termination requests succeed. Add coverage for a failed or interrupted terminate followed by retry.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/native-monitor/native-monitor-entry.component.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 54,\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Bind logout confirmation to the session that opened it\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The dialog subscription survives component destruction and calls session.logout() on whichever access is current when it closes. If the original access is cleared or the user navigates away and signs in again while the confirmation remains open, confirming the old dialog logs out the new session and navigates back to the monitor.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Capture the access identity when opening the dialog, cancel and close it when that access or component is retired, and verify the identity before logging out or navigating.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"rewrite-app/apps/web/src/app/native-monitor/native-monitor-entry.component.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 48,\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Cancel pending login navigation when the entry view is retired\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"submit awaits an unscoped login and then opens the sole claim. ngOnDestroy only unsubscribes from backend problems, so a delayed login or proof-of-work result can establish access and navigate back to the monitor after the user has left the entry view.\\\",\\n      \\\"recommendation\\\": \\\"Tie login and its continuation to the entry view's lifetime; cancel or invalidate pending authentication on destruction and avoid applying or navigating from a retired attempt.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"verified\\\": [\\n    \\\"Checked the actual base-to-head diff, current HEAD and tree, native monitor routes, session and request scopes, profile selection, signed-int64 serialization, polling, Booklet caching, controls, and relevant lifecycle tests against current source.\\\",\\n    \\\"Compared the finish-all and login behavior with the named read-only Original checkout and inspected the checked-in monitor scope and qualification limits.\\\",\\n    \\\"The supplied receipt reports completed base CI at ad92a086, historical published CI failures at 13b553, and later local evidence at fe4e882; none is a complete CI result for 5308c84. The cache-environment proof names 5d9ba6c as its pre-fix head.\\\",\\n    \\\"Earlier reported Goto context capture, slow Booklet enrichment, profile cancellation and timer input issues have corresponding changes in current source; their historical failures alone are not treated as current findings.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n    \\\"No current commit-matched CI or complete browser qualification was supplied, and broad suites were not rerun. Whole-project, visual and native participant transport parity remain unproven.\\\",\\n    \\\"Findings are based on source and control-flow inspection; the partial finish and stale authentication scenarios were not reproduced in a browser during this review.\\\",\\n    \\\"The repository Brain brief could not run because its lock directory could not be created in the read-only environment; direct source and documentation inspection was used instead.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a184d1-912e-70d0-9d86-694502899ef9","create_time":1793258604.693955}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
